MuNet
-----

The architecture code and frozen weights under
`src/muon_tomo/_vendor/munet/` are adapted from Muon-Tomography-AI, Copyright
2023 Lim Li Xin Jed and Qiu Ziming, licensed under Apache License 2.0:

https://github.com/jedlimlx/Muon-Tomography-AI

The copied upstream licence is retained in
`third_party/Muon-Tomography-AI-LICENSE`, and weight checksums are recorded in
`third_party/MUNET_WEIGHTS.sha256`.

Packaging changes use relative imports. The `Agg2D` constructor guard was also
corrected to compare the scattered feature count with the final MLP width; the
upstream tuple-form assertion was always true. This validation-only correction
does not alter inference for the packaged model configurations.

muonTruck
---------

The ROOT input adapter and the PoCA and likelihood/MLEM implementations are
derived from the local muonTruck research code at source revision
8393853a47e8654552a62d1886fb6766d637782f, with local uncommitted changes
present at import time. The upstream repository supplied by the project owner
is:

https://github.com/kfung010/muonTruck

The linked TFRecord generator is:

https://github.com/kfung010/muonTruck/blob/main/recon/generate_tfrecord.py

No licence file was found in the source used for the adaptation. The top-level
Apache licence does not grant rights to muonTruck-derived material.
Redistribution outside the owner's environment requires confirmation of the
applicable licence. The affected unified paths are:

- `src/muon_tomo/io/root.py`
- `src/muon_tomo/reconstruction/poca.py`
- `src/muon_tomo/reconstruction/likelihood.py`

All adapted components were changed to integrate the methods behind a shared
data model, fixed 64^3 geometry, explicit units, and one output schema.

Muons-Data-Generation
---------------------

The optional native backend in src/muon_tomo/simulation/geant4/main.cc is adapted
from the local Muon-Tomography-AI/Muons-Data-Generation-master implementation,
Copyright 2023 Lim Li Xin Jed and Qiu Ziming, under Apache License 2.0.
Its license is retained in third_party/Muons-Data-Generation-LICENSE.
Changes include canonical half-cell voxel placement, strict input checks,
portable headless operation, deterministic seeds, explicit CSV schema, exact
outgoing-plane recording, primary-only selection, and checked process status.
The old straight-ray rejection and hard-coded source paths are not retained.
Python scene construction, orchestration, validation and dataset manifests are
new unified-package integration code. This backend is independent of muonTruck.
